  "qid": "reviewUSC6Z2qYt8BXkwBa",
  "query": "As a researcher focused on large language models (LLMs), I am seeking a comprehensive literature review of recent reinforcement learning (RL) algorithms proposed to improve LLM reasoning capabilities beyond the GRPO approach. Please analyze the following 10 algorithms: DAPO (Decoupled Clip and Dynamic sAmpling Policy Optimization), GFPO (Group Filtered Policy Optimization), GMPO (Geometric-Mean Policy Optimization), GPPO (Gradient-Preserving clipping Policy Optimization), GPG (Group Policy Gradient), CPO (Comparative Policy Optimization), RPO (Reparameterization Proximal Policy Optimization), PPO (Proximal Policy Optimization), COPO (Consistency-Aware Policy Optimization), GSPO (Group Sequence Policy Optimization), covering:\n- Motivation and the core idea/innovation.\n- Key takeaways and claimed contributions.\n- Differences vs. GRPO\n- Empirical setup: model(s) used, training configs, compute budget, and evaluation benchmarks/datasets with results (include metrics and headline numbers where available).\n- Limitations and reported failure modes.\n\nPlease note that if full empirical details are not available for some algorithms, a summary of available information is sufficient. The goal is to capture current trends and insights to inform further research."
}
